# Build output. Everything the build produces lives under artifacts/ and none of it is committed.
/artifacts/

# Per-project intermediates, for anything that escapes the artifacts pivot.
[Bb]in/
[Oo]bj/

# COMPILED CONTENT IS A BUILD OUTPUT.
#
# assets/ holds what a human edits - the .png, .tga, .fbx, .wav, .mp3, .spritefont and the .fx
# shader sources, all of which Refactored Games released and all of which ARE in this repository.
# The .xnb the pipeline produces from them is not: it would make every texture tweak a binary
# diff, and it is reproducible from what is here. See license.md and assets/README.md.
#
# Two things still come from your own copy of the game, and neither can be derived from assets/:
# the shipped .xnb effect containers the GL shader build reuses for their parameter defaults, and
# the .wma music the transcode step converts. That is why a release is cut locally and not by CI.
/Content/
*.xnb

# A deployed installation, made by tools/build/40-deploy.sh. Disposable and rebuilt on demand -
# and it contains a copy of the game's compiled Content once you have run anything against it.
/game/

# The shader compiler: a pinned clone of our ShadowDusk fork plus natives from NuGet, assembled
# by tools/shadowdusk/build-shadowdusk.sh into artifacts/. Fetched, never vendored - 155 MB
# across all RIDs, and a 27 MB .so never delta-compresses, so committing it would add a full
# copy to history on every rebuild.
/tools/shadowdusk/bin/

# Player state, if someone runs the game from the tree.
/user/
/Saves/
Options.xml
ModSettings.xml

# Runtime droppings. A stale Errors.txt shipped in every package for weeks once, looking like a
# report on the build you had just made.
Errors.txt
RenderTrace.txt
/RenderTrace/

# Editors and OS
.vs/
.idea/
*.user
*.suo
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
